Whoa. whoa. whoa.

51
00:04:18.726 --> 00:04:20.987
What choice is
there? What choice?

52
00:04:21.011 --> 00:04:22.805
If you're in danger.
then it would be...

53
00:04:22.829 --> 00:04:25.241
Wait. wait. stop. stop. Stop.

54
00:04:25.265 --> 00:04:28.043
You keep saying that
word. "Danger." "Danger."

55
00:04:28.067 --> 00:04:30.880
But you said... No. I
have never used that word.

56
00:04:30.904 --> 00:04:34.016
I said "complicated." and
then you flew off the handle.

57
00:04:34.040 --> 00:04:37.287
Yeah. I flew off the
handle when I saw that.

58
00:04:37.311 --> 00:04:40.206
Okay? Where'd
that come from? Hm?

59
00:04:40.230 --> 00:04:43.176
A fall in the shower? Uh...

60
00:04:43.200 --> 00:04:47.213
This is just so
passive-aggressive. you know.

61
00:04:47.237 --> 00:04:48.714
Passive-aggressive?

62
00:04:48.738 --> 00:04:52.318
I go two days without returning
your phone calls. two days.

63
00:04:52.342 --> 00:04:55.621
and I have one
minor little incident.

64
00:04:55.645 --> 00:04:57.056
and now you're telling me

65
00:04:57.080 --> 00:04:59.658
that I should turn
myself in to the police!

66
00:04:59.682 --> 00:05:01.060
A minor incident? Yes.

67
00:05:01.084 --> 00:05:03.902
What minor little incident?

68
00:05:05.105 --> 00:05:10.258
I had an argument
with a co-worker. okay?

69
00:05:11.678 --> 00:05:13.739
And?

70
00:05:13.763 --> 00:05:15.007
I had an argument.

71
00:05:15.031 --> 00:05:17.077
We were in this bar

72
00:05:17.101 --> 00:05:20.413
and we were discussing a
particular business strategy.

73
00:05:20.437 --> 00:05:26.619
And it got heated and out of
control. and he hit me. Once.

74
00:05:26.643 --> 00:05:29.956
And I didn't retaliate because
he's a much older man.

75
00:05:29.980 --> 00:05:32.280
And that's it.

76
00:05:34.702 --> 00:05:37.118
You were in a bar fight?

77
00:05:39.806 --> 00:05:45.126
Yes. Skyler. I
was in a bar fight.

78
00:05:46.446 --> 00:05:48.613
So you're okay?

79
00:05:50.483 --> 00:05:52.150
Really?

80
00:05:55.872 --> 00:05:57.517
Yes.

81
00:05:57.541 --> 00:05:59.290
I'm okay.

82
00:06:00.944 --> 00:06:02.255
And I think. in the end.

83
00:06:02.279 --> 00:06:04.456
that it may have
been a good thing

84
00:06:04.480 --> 00:06:07.810
because we were able to
clear the air and. you know...

85
00:06:07.834 --> 00:06:10.596
Mutual respect. and...

86
00:06:10.620 --> 00:06:12.303
So...

87
00:06:13.524 --> 00:06:15.489
Frozen peas.

88
00:06:17.560 --> 00:06:18.855
What?

89
00:06:18.879 --> 00:06:20.490
It's the best thing
for the swelling.

90
00:06:20.514 --> 00:06:24.193
Oh. it's not really
swollen. it's just...

91
00:06:24.217 --> 00:06:26.780
No peas.

92
00:06:26.804 --> 00:06:28.381
You don't even have ice.

93
00:06:28.405 --> 00:06:30.716
I will get peas. I will get ice.

94
00:06:30.740 --> 00:06:32.673
Peas and ice.
I'm writing it down.

95
00:06:34.228 --> 00:06:35.693
I. um...

96
00:06:37.898 --> 00:06:41.461
I need you to promise me

97
00:06:41.485 --> 00:06:45.197
that if things do
get dangerous...

98
00:06:45.221 --> 00:06:47.984
Skyler... Promise me.

99
00:06:48.008 --> 00:06:50.158
Absolutely.

100
00:06:52.696 --> 00:06:54.112
So...

101
00:06:55.531 --> 00:06:58.094
Car wash.

102
00:06:58.118 --> 00:07:00.546
[OVER SPEAKERS] <i> ♪
Trouble. kiss me again ♪</i>

103
00:07:00.570 --> 00:07:02.682
<i>♪ 'Cause I'm hoping you are ♪</i>

104
00:07:02.706 --> 00:07:06.102
<i>♪ Press it right there And
I'll pay you back double ♪</i>

105
00:07:06.126 --> 00:07:11.657
<i>♪ But this ain't the real
thing Look at my lips ♪</i>

106
00:07:11.681 --> 00:07:14.060
WOMAN: Honey. Charles.

107
00:07:14.084 --> 00:07:17.763
<i>♪ Look at my teeth
They're just aching to bite ♪</i>

108
00:07:17.787 --> 00:07:19.565
Take a look at this kitchen.

109
00:07:19.589 --> 00:07:22.668
<i>♪ It's a big empty chasm ♪</i>

110
00:07:22.692 --> 00:07:25.938
Hi there. Can I
answer any questions?

111
00:07:25.962 --> 00:07:28.625
Yes. Any chance of a top-off?

112
00:07:28.649 --> 00:07:31.366
Oh. I think we can
help you out there.

113
00:07:33.770 --> 00:07:37.906
<i>♪ You've got compassion
Coming out of your ears ♪</i>

114
00:07:39.076 --> 00:07:41.620
So. what do you think?

115
00:07:41.644 --> 00:07:44.941
Oh. very nice. Very open.

116
00:07:44.965 --> 00:07:47.410
Oh. I agree. It flows. Mm.

117
00:07:47.434 --> 00:07:49.813
Whole lot of natural light.

118
00:07:49.837 --> 00:07:51.314
Michael Kilbourne.

119
00:07:51.338 --> 00:07:54.083
Tori Costner. It's
nice to meet you.

120
00:07:54.107 --> 00:07:56.519
Well. three bedrooms.
one and a half baths

121
00:07:56.543 --> 00:07:58.071
on just under half an acre.

122
00:07:58.095 --> 00:08:01.040
There's a non-attached
casita out in back.

123
00:08:01.064 --> 00:08:04.143
Permit usable as
office or guest suite.

124
00:08:04.167 --> 00:08:06.379
Hm. Plank wood floors.

125
00:08:06.403 --> 00:08:08.464
Central heat and air.

126
00:08:08.488 --> 00:08:10.333
I see you're married.

127
00:08:10.357 --> 00:08:12.134
No. divorced.

128
00:08:12.158 --> 00:08:13.636
Very recent.

129
00:08:13.660 --> 00:08:15.755
Old habits. Oh. I'm sorry.

130
00:08:15.779 --> 00:08:17.190
But any children?

131
00:08:17.214 --> 00:08:19.392
Yes. as a matter
of fact. A little boy.

132
00:08:19.416 --> 00:08:21.060
Oh. how old?

133
00:08:21.084 --> 00:08:22.495
He turned 4 in May.

134
00:08:22.519 --> 00:08:24.446
He's a Gemini.
Would love this yard.

135
00:08:24.470 --> 00:08:26.649
Oh. plenty of space
for a jungle gym.

136
00:08:26.673 --> 00:08:29.685
And the neighborhood
preschool is fantastic.

137
00:08:29.709 --> 00:08:32.137
I think Eli is going
to be homeschooled.

138
00:08:32.161 --> 00:08:34.507
Oh. well. great. Not
for religious reasons.

139
00:08:34.531 --> 00:08:37.126
I wanna make sure
he's getting attention.

140
00:08:37.150 --> 00:08:40.196
He'll still go to summer
camp and whatnot. playdates.

141
00:08:40.220 --> 00:08:41.947
Don't want him to
be socially awkward.

142
00:08:41.971 --> 00:08:43.733
Oh. no. Makes sense.

143
00:08:43.757 --> 00:08:46.819
He tests very
highly. 96 percentile.

144
00:08:46.843 --> 00:08:49.505
But that whole
right brain. left brain.

145
00:08:49.529 --> 00:08:51.124
You want those in balance.

146
00:08:51.148 --> 00:08:52.397
Oh. yeah.

147
00:08:53.500 --> 00:08:57.297
You said the casita
has plumbing?

148
00:08:57.321 --> 00:08:58.831
I work a lot with clay.

149
00:08:58.855 --> 00:09:01.467
so I need access
to running water.

150
00:09:01.491 --> 00:09:04.636
Well. it's pipe-fitted
for a quarter bath so...

151
00:09:04.660 --> 00:09:07.806
Make a perfect studio.

152
00:09:07.830 --> 00:09:09.842
Hm.

153
00:09:09.866 --> 00:09:12.595
This could work.

154
00:09:12.619 --> 00:09:15.181
<i>Heh. heh. Hell.
that's the doctor's plan</i>

155
00:09:15.205 --> 00:09:17.299
<i>to get her patients at ease.</i>

156
00:09:17.323 --> 00:09:19.168
<i>If you know what I mean.</i>

157
00:09:19.192 --> 00:09:20.652
WOMAN 1: <i>But. nurse...</i>

158
00:09:20.676 --> 00:09:22.805
MARIE: Hello? I'm back.

159
00:09:22.829 --> 00:09:24.507
WOMAN 2: <i>That's okay.</i>

160
00:09:24.531 --> 00:09:26.998
MARIE: Hank? Yeah.

161
00:09:30.903 --> 00:09:32.837
[HANK CLEARS THROAT]

162
00:09:34.841 --> 00:09:37.553
I had to go to three places

163
00:09:37.577 --> 00:09:39.989
to get the moisturizer
that you like. But I got that.

164
00:09:40.013 --> 00:09:44.227
And I got your Shiner
Bock and your chips.

165
00:09:44.251 --> 00:09:47.351
And I couldn't resist.

166
00:09:49.289 --> 00:09:52.769
The complete encyclopedia
to fantasy football.

167
00:09:52.793 --> 00:09:54.570
Look. it has all
the latest rankings.

168
00:09:54.594 --> 00:09:57.395
Marie. I said
Cheetos. not Fritos.

169
00:09:58.715 --> 00:10:00.193
Wait. I...

170
00:10:00.217 --> 00:10:03.612
I said Cheetos. like. 10 times.
You need me to write it down?

171
00:10:03.636 --> 00:10:06.666
No. and I don't need you
to be mean about it either.

172
00:10:06.690 --> 00:10:08.200
Well. I'm just saying. you know.

173
00:10:08.224 --> 00:10:10.837
I said Cheetos.
"Ch." "ch." "ch" sound.

174
00:10:10.861 --> 00:10:14.189
Virtually impossible to
confuse Cheetos with Fritos.

175
00:10:14.213 --> 00:10:16.358
seems to me.
Where are you going?

176
00:10:16.382 --> 00:10:19.316
I... Back to the store. I guess.

177
00:10:20.486 --> 00:10:22.197
Here.

178
00:10:22.221 --> 00:10:25.040
And the draft's not for two
months. so this is useless.

179
00:10:26.276 --> 00:10:28.143
[DOOR OPENS]

180
00:10:30.097 --> 00:10:31.262
[DOOR CLOSES]

181
00:10:38.955 --> 00:10:40.922
Can you believe it?

182
00:10:42.759 --> 00:10:44.737
What?

183
00:10:44.761 --> 00:10:47.095
What? This.

184
00:10:51.734 --> 00:10:54.780
Well. you always said
this place could be bugged.

185
00:10:54.804 --> 00:10:57.433
Now we know. Yeah. well.

186
00:10:57.457 --> 00:10:59.252
I don't like it.

187
00:10:59.276 --> 00:11:01.743
It's a violation of
the work space.

188
00:11:03.079 --> 00:11:04.612
Yeah. I guess.

189
00:11:05.848 --> 00:11:08.015
You wanna do something?

190
00:11:09.452 --> 00:11:11.063
Do something?

191
00:11:11.087 --> 00:11:12.720
Like what?

192
00:11:14.357 --> 00:11:16.357
Go-karts?

193
00:11:18.611 --> 00:11:20.440
Go-karts. What...?

194
00:11:20.464 --> 00:11:25.811
Yeah. there's a track
down by the Coliseum.

195
00:11:25.835 --> 00:11:27.802
It's pretty fun.

196
00:11:31.440 --> 00:11:38.941
No. actually I have some
kind of a meeting. so...

197
00:11:38.965 --> 00:11:40.131
All right. whatever.

198
00:11:44.470 --> 00:11:45.981
Rain check?

199
00:11:46.005 --> 00:11:48.405
Yeah. Sure.

200
00:11:54.313 --> 00:11:56.147
How you doing?

201
00:11:57.516 --> 00:12:00.151
Good. Yeah?

202
00:12:01.520 --> 00:12:03.454
You okay?

203
00:12:05.024 --> 00:12:09.526
Is there. uh. anything
we should talk about?

204
00:12:14.267 --> 00:12:16.167
How's your eye?

205
00:12:18.538 --> 00:12:21.217
Yeah. it's fine.

206
00:12:21.241 --> 00:12:25.376
Anything we should talk about?

207
00:12:32.335 --> 00:12:35.047
For what it's worth.

208
00:12:35.071 --> 00:12:38.601
getting the shit
kicked out of you...

209
00:12:38.625 --> 00:12:42.359
not to say you get used to it...

210
00:12:43.630 --> 00:12:46.347
but you do kind
of get used to it.

211
00:12:59.396 --> 00:13:02.524
Two words: nail salon.

212
00:13:02.548 --> 00:13:04.293
Perfect for money laundering.

213
00:13:04.317 --> 00:13:07.563
It's a high-volume business
with a discreet work force.

214
00:13:07.587 --> 00:13:10.415
I mean. nobody does.
"Mister. me know nothing"

215
00:13:10.439 --> 00:13:13.085
better than Mrs.
Mookjaiaporn and her gals.

216
00:13:13.109 --> 00:13:14.753
Mr. Goodman...

217
00:13:14.777 --> 00:13:16.022
"Saul." please.

218
00:13:16.046 --> 00:13:18.391
Now. for the lady of the house.

219
00:13:18.415 --> 00:13:20.860
Drum roll. How
about a lifetime supply

220
00:13:20.884 --> 00:13:23.328
of French manicures
and enzyme peels?

221
00:13:23.352 --> 00:13:25.647
Oh. yeah. go ahead.
Pinch yourself. Ha-ha-ha.

222
00:13:25.671 --> 00:13:29.085
We're not buying a nail
salon. Mr. Goodman.

223
00:13:29.109 --> 00:13:31.404
We're getting the car
wash. SAUL: I'm sorry.

224
00:13:31.428 --> 00:13:34.874
Am I missing something
here? Didn't you already try that?

225
00:13:34.898 --> 00:13:37.243
Yeah. I mean. Walt told me

226
00:13:37.267 --> 00:13:39.545
that you took a run at
this Bogdan character

227
00:13:39.569 --> 00:13:42.832
and he wrestled you into
submission with his eyebrows.

228
00:13:42.856 --> 00:13:45.984
Ten million. that was
the asking price. right?

229
00:13:46.008 --> 00:13:48.070
Apparently. he upped it to 20.

230
00:13:48.094 --> 00:13:50.056
Wow. Nice negotiating.

231
00:13:50.080 --> 00:13:53.609
Yeah. I mean. hey.
you bombed. It happens.

232
00:13:53.633 --> 00:13:56.779
You were smart
to call me. Now...

233
00:13:56.803 --> 00:14:00.249
You just sit back. relax. and
let a professional take over.

234
00:14:00.273 --> 00:14:01.517
[KNOCKING ON DOOR]

235
00:14:01.541 --> 00:14:04.309
That's for me. Excuse me.

236
00:14:08.298 --> 00:14:10.675
What do you want?
I'm in a meeting.

237
00:14:10.699 --> 00:14:13.896
Why didn't you think of
that before? It's not my...

238
00:14:13.920 --> 00:14:15.953
I'm in a meeting.

239
00:14:18.158 --> 00:14:20.453
Can Huell use your bathroom?

240
00:14:20.477 --> 00:14:23.823
Huell?

241
00:14:23.847 --> 00:14:26.926
Uh. sure. The top of the stairs.

242
00:14:26.950 --> 00:14:28.816
He'll be quick.

243
00:14:31.687 --> 00:14:33.665
It's a stomach thing. It's...

244
00:14:33.689 --> 00:14:35.801
So where were we?

245
00:14:35.825 --> 00:14:38.804
Professionalism. Yeah.

246
00:14:38.828 --> 00:14:41.490
So if the guy won't
sell. he won't sell.

247
00:14:41.514 --> 00:14:44.643
I don't accept that. I don't
accept that he won't sell.

248
00:14:44.667 --> 00:14:48.046
I think he just
lacks the proper...

249
00:14:48.070 --> 00:14:49.381
motivation.

250
00:14:49.405 --> 00:14:52.384
Motivation. Ah.

251
00:14:52.408 --> 00:14:56.788
As in "motivation" motivation?

252
00:14:56.812 --> 00:14:58.623
I mean. just so we're
on the same page here.

253
00:14:58.647 --> 00:15:01.793
are you saying we make
him an offer he can't refuse?

254
00:15:01.817 --> 00:15:04.446
SKYLER: Nothing so
dramatic as that. no.

255
00:15:04.470 --> 00:15:06.270
Motivation.

256
00:15:08.875 --> 00:15:10.769
Attitude adjustment.

257
00:15:10.793 --> 00:15:13.322
[LAUGHS]

258
00:15:13.346 --> 00:15:16.625
